{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ES2WBKaYSaRcPinDsCBRt9","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Round 2 spec-context analysis","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:spec-context-analyst","prompt":"You are participating in a speckit-autopilot consensus protocol Round 2 for a /speckit.clarify question. The codebase-analyst (Round 1) returned \"no precedent\" — there is no existing rate-limiter middleware in the codebase to extend. Your job is to analyze the project constitution, technical roadmap, and prior spec artifacts (spec.md, plan.md if present) to provide an answer grounded in established project decisions and principles.\n\nQuestion to resolve:\n\"Should we extend the existing rate-limiter middleware or write a new one for the new endpoint?\"\n\nWhat to check:\n1. Read the constitution.md (typically at .specify/memory/constitution.md or similar) — look for principles around middleware design, dependency choices, \"build vs. buy\", or non-functional requirements like rate limiting / abuse prevention.\n2. Read the current feature's spec.md — does it specify rate-limiting requirements (RPS limits, error responses, scope per-user vs. per-IP)?\n3. Read plan.md if it exists — has a technical approach already been chosen?\n4. Check the technical roadmap (docs/ai/roadmap or similar) for any prior or future specs that introduce rate limiting more broadly. If a separate spec is planned that would establish a project-wide rate-limiter, that constrains the answer for this feature.\n\nReturn a structured response with:\n1. Direct answer to the question grounded in project artifacts\n2. File-level citations (path + relevant excerpt)\n3. Confidence level (high/medium/low) and why\n4. Flag any conflicts between what spec.md asks for and what the constitution allows\n\nDo not write files. Do not edit code. Return your analysis as the tool result."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
